WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.009
I'm often given tasks on the fly whereas
many of my tasks are given as a result

00:00:05.009 --> 00:00:10.469
of meetings these days an increasing
number are coming from emails or my

00:00:10.469 --> 00:00:13.590
manager or client asking me to do
something I find myself quite

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:19.710
disorganized when dealing with this I'm
writing things down when I'm told but

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:24.060
it's all over the place
post-its notebook phone etc I don't have

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:27.720
a solid method of keeping track of these
things I'm guessing that a possible

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.199
solution is to write all these things
down in the same place but I've also

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:35.309
tried that and didn't really make a
difference I'd appreciate any input or

00:00:35.309 --> 00:00:39.570
advice you have on how to record and
track objectives in a functional in a

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:45.510
reliable manner as I'm subjected to a
lot of information each day week month

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:49.039
I'm definitely overloaded to remember it
myself

00:00:49.039 --> 00:00:53.969
discipline equals freedom so yeah a few
things first first of all definitely

00:00:53.969 --> 00:00:59.010
write the things down in one place and
it sounds like since you're moving all

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.250
the time or you're going to meetings
carry out just a nice little notebook

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:06.990
with you and write the things down as
you get tasked with them then on top of

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:12.540
that you have to have a master list of
some kind either paper or digital I'm

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:17.880
gonna probably recommend digital to
track things overall in a prioritized

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.970
method so if you get tasks something in
a meeting in your little notebook you

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:29.430
come back you put it in the right place
in the master task list and then like

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:34.200
twice a day to consolidate the
information that's in the little

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:39.900
notebook you have into the big master
list and then before you go to bed at

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:44.549
night you organize those things by
priority on the master list you put the

00:01:44.549 --> 00:01:47.820
most important thing at the top and
that's what you're going to attack the

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:53.040
next day that's part one on how you get
these things organized now the part two

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.000
is you've got to schedule this stuff and
actually I always say this when people

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:02.430
have trouble with tasks put them on the
calendar to you know actually Jamie does

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:06.240
that for me when Jamie's got something
for me to do she just doesn't email me

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.300
and say hey you need to do this she puts
it on the calendar so I look at my

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.620
calendar boom there it is I gotta go do
this what

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:17.909
this task is done so put these things on
your calendar and that includes

00:02:17.909 --> 00:02:23.230
scheduling time on your calendar so that
you can have time to consolidate your

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:27.310
list and do a review of your lists you
know whether that takes that probably

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:33.970
take 15 minutes to do and I guess
there's a bunch of apps you can use and

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:36.569
I'm sure people will make
recommendations but there's a ton of

00:02:36.569 --> 00:02:41.650
to-do list apps including there's one
there's native ones on all the different

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:46.629
phones so you could look at that as it
possible a voice recorder you can either

00:02:46.629 --> 00:02:50.170
use the voice recorder app you have or
you can carry around a little mini voice

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:53.920
recorder then you can just take notes
with that and then you consolidate those

00:02:53.920 --> 00:03:01.450
notes from your from your voice recorder
into your master task list every day and

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:09.299
then you just kind of prioritize and
execute it's it pretty straightforward

